# WBooks frontend: no environment variables or credentials are required.
# This file intentionally contains no secrets and no required assignments.
# A .env file is optional, ignored by Git, and must never contain real credentials
# intended for browser code. Every VITE_* variable is public in the built app.
#
# Optional browser-test override, supplied in your shell (not loaded from .env):
# CHROMIUM_PATH=/path/to/chromium npm run test:e2e
#
# Never add GitHub tokens, passwords, private keys, or database credentials here.
# Use GitHub CLI's interactive authentication for GitHub operations.
